<worksheet xml:id="writing-assignment-5">
<title>Writing Assignment 5: Pattern Types, Quadratic Forms, and Revenue Models</title>

<introduction>
<p>This assignment asks you to classify patterns from data, move between the three forms of a quadratic, and interpret a quadratic revenue model in context.</p>
<p>Show every algebraic step. A final answer with no supporting work earns no credit.</p>
<p>In Question 1, your justification must include the actual differences or ratios you computed, not just the name of the pattern.</p>
<p>In Question 2, show which point you substituted each time you solve for the leading coefficient.</p>
<p>Every answer that asks for an interpretation should be written in a complete sentence, in context, with units.</p>
<p>Upload a clean, high-quality scan of your pages to Blackboard when complete.</p>
</introduction>

<page>
<exercise xml:id="wa5-classify">
<title>Classifying Three Patterns</title>
<introduction>
<p>
Each table below shows a relationship between
<m>x</m>
and
<m>y</m>
. Exactly one of the three is linear, one is exponential, and one is quadratic, but they are not listed in that order.
</p>
<p>
For each data set, run all three tests: first differences, second differences, and ratios of consecutive outputs. Show the values you computed.
</p>
</introduction>

