<task workspace="2in">
<statement>
<p>
Compare your three predictions at
<m>x = 8</m>
. One of them is negative and one of them is enormous. In two or three complete sentences, explain what those two results say about how each type of pattern behaves as
<m>x</m>
grows, and describe a situation where the negative output would mean the model has stopped making sense.
</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task workspace="1.5in">
<statement>
<p>
Suppose a fourth data set had first differences that were not constant, second differences that were not constant, and ratios that were not constant. What would you conclude, and what would you still be able to say about the data? Answer in complete sentences.
</p>
</statement>
</task>
</exercise>
