<page>
<exercise xml:id="wa5-three-forms">
<title>Three Forms of a Quadratic from a Graph</title>
<introduction>
<p>
The graph of a quadratic function
<m>f</m>
is shown below. The horizontal intercepts, the vertical intercept, and the vertex all occur at integer coordinates.
</p>
<image width="55%">
<shortdescription>An upward opening parabola with horizontal intercepts at negative one and three, a vertical intercept at zero comma negative six, and a vertex at one comma negative eight.</shortdescription>
<description>
<p>A parabola opening upward on a coordinate grid. It crosses the horizontal axis at negative one comma zero and three comma zero, crosses the vertical axis at zero comma negative six, and reaches its lowest point at one comma negative eight.</p>
</description>
<prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="wa5-parabola">
<diagram dimensions="(320,256)" margins="5">
<definition>f(x) = 2*(x+1)*(x-3)</definition>
<coordinates bbox="(-4,-10,6,6)">
<grid-axes xlabel="x" ylabel="y" spacings="((-4,1,6),(-10,2,6))"/>
<graph function="f" domain="(-1.65,3.65)" stroke="blue" thickness="2"/>
<point p="(-1,0)" alignment="nw">
<m>(-1,0)</m>
</point>
<point p="(3,0)" alignment="ne">
<m>(3,0)</m>
</point>
<point p="(0,-6)" alignment="e">
<m>(0,-6)</m>
</point>
<point p="(1,-8)" alignment="s">
<m>(1,-8)</m>
</point>
</coordinates>
</diagram>
</prefigure>
</image>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1.5in">
<statement>
<p>
List the horizontal intercepts, the vertical intercept, and the vertex. State whether the parabola opens upward or downward, and explain what that tells you about the sign of the leading coefficient
<m>a</m>
before you compute anything.
</p>
</statement>
</task>

