<page>
<exercise xml:id="wa5-revenue">
<title>A Revenue Model for a Price Change</title>
<introduction>
<p>
A campus bookstore currently sells its logo water bottle for
<m>\$10</m>
. The manager is considering changing the price and models the store's weekly revenue with the function
</p>
<p>
<m>R(x) = -10(x + 10)(x - 50),</m>
</p>
<p>
where
<m>x</m>
is the <term>change in price</term> in dollars from the current
<m>\$10</m>
, and
<m>R(x)</m>
is the weekly revenue in dollars. A positive
<m>x</m>
means the price goes up and a negative
<m>x</m>
means the price goes down. For example,
<m>x = 4</m>
corresponds to a new price of
<m>\$14</m>
.
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="2in">
<statement>
<p>
Show that
<m>R(x)</m>
can also be written as
<m>R(x) = (10 + x)(500 - 10x)</m>
by expanding both expressions and comparing them.
</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task workspace="1.75in">
<statement>
<p>
Using the form from part (a), explain what each factor represents in this situation. Your answer should say how many bottles the store currently sells each week, and how the number sold changes for every dollar the price goes up. Write in complete sentences.
</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task workspace="1.5in">
<statement>
<p>
Find
<m>R(0)</m>
and explain what it means for the bookstore.
</p>
<p>
<m>R(0) =</m>
<fillin characters="12"/>
</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task workspace="2.25in">
<statement>
<p>
Write
<m>R(x)</m>
in general form and in vertex form. Show the work for each.
</p>
<p>
General form:
<fillin characters="22"/>
</p>
<p>
Vertex form:
<fillin characters="22"/>
</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task workspace="2.25in">
<statement>
<p>
Find the horizontal intercepts of
<m>R</m>
. For each one, state the price the bookstore would be charging and explain in a complete sentence why the revenue is zero at that price. The two explanations should be different from each other.
</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task workspace="2in">
<statement>
<p>
Find the vertex of
<m>R</m>
. Then answer all three of the following: what price should the bookstore charge, how many bottles will it sell per week at that price, and what is the maximum weekly revenue?
</p>
<p>
Price:
<fillin characters="10"/>
Bottles:
<fillin characters="10"/>
Revenue:
<fillin characters="10"/>
</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task workspace="2.75in">
<statement>
<p>
Solve
<m>R(x) = 8000</m>
algebraically. Show every step. Then interpret both solutions: state the price associated with each, and explain in a complete sentence why two different prices can produce the same weekly revenue.
</p>
<p>
<m>x =</m>
<fillin characters="16"/>
</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task workspace="1.75in">
<statement>
<p>
What values of
<m>x</m>
make sense as inputs in this situation? Justify your answer using both the algebra and the context, and identify at least one value of
<m>x</m>
that the function will happily evaluate but that the bookstore could never actually use.
</p>
</statement>
</task>

<task workspace="1in">
